# Error Handling

## Never Swallow Errors

Empty or silent catch blocks are forbidden. Every caught error must either be re-thrown, logged to Sentry, or surfaced to the user — usually all three.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
try {
  await deleteSpot(spotId);
} catch (error) {
  console.error(error);
}

// ✅ GOOD
try {
  await deleteSpot(spotId);
} catch (error) {
  Sentry.captureException(error);
  showToast('Could not delete spot. Please try again.');
}
```

## Always Pair Loading with Error

Every piece of UI that shows a loading state must also handle the error state. Never render a loading spinner with no error fallback.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
const { data: spots, isLoading } = useSpots(cityId);
if (isLoading) return <LoadingSpinner />;
return <SpotList spots={spots} />;

// ✅ GOOD
const { data: spots, isLoading, error } = useSpots(cityId);
if (isLoading) return <LoadingSpinner />;
if (error) return <ErrorState message="Could not load spots." onRetry={refetch} />;
return <SpotList spots={spots} />;
```

## React Query Mutations

Mutations must define `onError`. The error must reach the user, not just the console.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
const mutation = useMutation({ mutationFn: createSpot });

// ✅ GOOD
const mutation = useMutation({
  mutationFn: createSpot,
  onSuccess: () => {
    queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['spots', cityId] });
    router.back();
  },
  onError: (error) => {
    Sentry.captureException(error);
    showToast('Could not save spot. Please try again.');
  },
});
```

## Supabase API Layer

Check and throw on every Supabase response. Never let `error` be silently ignored. Return typed data only on success.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
const { data } = await supabase.from('spots').select('*');
return data;

// ✅ GOOD
const { data, error } = await supabase.from('spots').select('*');
if (error) throw error;
return data;
```

## Two Types of Errors — Handle Them Differently

**User errors** (validation, empty fields, bad input) — handled by `react-hook-form` + Zod inline. Do not log to Sentry.
**System errors** (network, Supabase failure, timeout) — log to Sentry and show a toast via `react-native-toast-message`. Never expose raw error messages or stack traces to the user.

```tsx
import Toast from 'react-native-toast-message';

// ✅ GOOD — validation error (react-hook-form handles inline, no Sentry)
// Zod schema catches this before submission

// ✅ GOOD — system error (Sentry + toast)
} catch (error) {
  Sentry.captureException(error, { extra: { action: 'createSpot' } });
  Toast.show({ type: 'error', text1: 'Could not save spot', text2: 'Please try again.' });
}
```

## Async Functions Must Be Fully Handled

Every `async` function called from a component or event handler must have its errors caught. Unhandled promise rejections crash silently on some platforms.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<Button onPress={() => handleSave()} />

// ✅ GOOD — handleSave is async and has its own try/catch
const handleSave = async () => {
  try {
    await saveSpot(formData);
    router.back();
  } catch (error) {
    Sentry.captureException(error, { extra: { action: 'saveSpot' } });
    Toast.show({ type: 'error', text1: 'Could not save', text2: 'Please try again.' });
  }
};
```

## Error Boundaries

Wrap each major screen section in a React error boundary to prevent a rendering crash from taking down the whole app. A single root-level boundary in `app/_layout.tsx` is the minimum — add screen-level boundaries for complex screens.

## Sentry Usage

Log to Sentry for all system errors. Add context so the error is actionable in the dashboard.

```ts
// ✅ GOOD — context makes the error traceable
Sentry.captureException(error, {
  extra: { spotId, cityId, action: 'createSpot' },
});
```

Never log to Sentry for validation failures, empty states, or user cancellations.

## Toast Usage

Use `react-native-toast-message` (`Toast.show`) for all system-level user feedback. Validation errors are shown inline by react-hook-form — do not use a toast for them.

```ts
// Success
Toast.show({ type: 'success', text1: 'Spot saved' });

// Error
Toast.show({ type: 'error', text1: 'Could not save spot', text2: 'Please try again.' });
```

`<Toast />` is mounted once in `app/_layout.tsx` — do not mount it per-screen.
